  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The component implements a functional image carousel with native buttons and dynamic `alt` text, but it omits core WAI-ARIA Carousel pattern requirements. Most critically, it lacks an `aria-live` region to announce state changes, missing the carousel landmark/role context, and provides no programmatic active state for indicators. These are design gaps that cause screen reader users to lose track of progress and fail to recognize the widget's interaction model. Automated checks will likely pass because native `<button>` elements and `alt` attributes satisfy baseline compliance, but assistive technology users will experience a broken dynamic content flow.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**:\nBased on the component type and title (\"Without Region and Live Region\"), I predicted:\n1. Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic image updates (state communication gap)\n2. Missing landmark/role context (`aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"` or `<figure>`)\n3. Indicators lacking programmatic active state (`aria-selected`/`aria-current`)\n4. Missing keyboard navigation pattern (arrow keys per APG Carousel)\n5. Focus management undefined for indicator interaction\n\nActual findings align with all predictions. The component is a standard state-driven slideshow that treats dynamic DOM updates as visual-only, violating the WAI-ARIA Carousel pattern's requirement for programmatic status announcements and landmark context.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings (blocks access)\n*None. The component does not block access entirely; mouse/touch interaction and native button semantics provide a functional baseline.*\n\n### Major Findings (significantly degrades experience)\n\n1. **Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic image changes**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:14` (`<img src={images[currentIndex]} alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} />`) updates dynamically via React state, but no live region announces the change.\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages); WAI-ARIA Carousel Pattern requires a status region with `aria-live=\"polite\"` to announce current slide position and total count.\n   - **Fix**: Add `<div aria-live=\"polite\" className=\"sr-only\">Image {currentIndex + 1} of {images.length}</div>` inside the carousel container. Update this region's text on index change rather than relying solely on `alt` updates, which screen readers often ignore or announce inconsistently during rapid state changes.\n\n2. **Missing carousel landmark/role context**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:12` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`) and surrounding structure use generic `<div>` elements without semantic grouping.\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users, keyboard users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WAI-ARIA Carousel Pattern; WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value). The pattern requires `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"` on the container to establish widget context and enable AT-specific navigation shortcuts.\n   - **Fix**: Replace the outer `<div>` with `<figure aria-roledescription=\"carousel\" className=\"carousel\">` or add `role=\"region\" aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"`. This signals to assistive technology that the contained buttons and images form a single interactive widget.\n\n3. **Indicator buttons lack programmatic active state**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:28-34` (`className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}`) relies solely on CSS for visual feedback. No ARIA attribute communicates selection to AT.\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Screen reader users, cognitive accessibility users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WAI-ARIA Carousel Pattern; WCAG 4.1.2. Indicator buttons must use `aria-selected={idx === currentIndex}` or `aria-current=\"true\"` so screen readers announce the active state programmatically.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-selected={idx === currentIndex}` to each indicator `<button>`. Ensure CSS styles for `.active` and `[aria-selected=\"true\"]` are synchronized.\n\n4. **Missing keyboard navigation pattern (arrow keys)**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:6-10` only implements `onClick` handlers. No `onKeyDown` or arrow key routing is present.\n   - **User Group Impacted**: Keyboard-only users, motor accessibility users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard); WAI-ARIA Carousel Pattern requires Left/Right arrow keys to navigate slides when focus is within the carousel.\n   - **Fix**: Add `onKeyDown` to the carousel container or indicator buttons. Route `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` to `goToPrevious()`/`goToNext()`. Prevent default to avoid page scrolling. Document that arrow keys control the carousel per APG.\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings (friction but workaround exists)\n- **Alt text updates are insufficient for dynamic content**: While `alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`}` changes, screen readers do not consistently announce `alt` attribute mutations during state updates. Relying on `alt` alone is a known anti-pattern for dynamic carousels. (WCAG 4.1.3)\n- **Indicator button text is purely numeric**: `{idx + 1}` provides no context to keyboard users who tab through indicators. Screen readers will announce \"One\", \"Two\", etc., without indicating these are slide controls. Add `aria-label={`Go to slide ${idx + 1} of ${images.length}`} ` for clarity.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions)\n- **Missing `aria-roledescription`**: Screen readers won't announce \"carousel\" context, missing pattern-specific navigation hints.\n- **Missing live region**: Dynamic state changes are visually apparent but programmatic silence breaks screen reader flow.\n- **Missing keyboard routing**: Carousels are expected to support arrow keys; without it, keyboard users must tab through every button or rely on click/touch only.\n- **Missing focus management for indicators**: When navigating via arrow keys (once implemented), focus should move to the corresponding indicator button or stay within the carousel widget per roving tabindex conventions.\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | HIGH | Missing live region, missing carousel role, indicators lack `aria-selected` |\n| Keyboard-only | MEDIUM | No arrow key navigation; tab order works but widget pattern is incomplete |\n| Low vision | LOW | Visual structure is intact; focus visibility depends on external CSS not shown |\n| Cognitive | MEDIUM | Progress tracking relies on visual indicators only; no programmatic state sync |\n| Vestibular & motion | LOW | No animations/transitions present in code |\n| Auditory access | LOW | No media/audio elements |\n| Environmental contrast | LOW | Visual-only active state depends on external CSS; not verifiable here |\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\nThe component passes baseline automated checks because it uses native `<button>` elements and provides `alt` text. However, the accessibility *design* is incomplete per the WAI-ARIA Carousel pattern. The absence of an `aria-live` region means screen reader users cannot track progress in a multi-slide carousel. The missing `aria-roledescription` prevents assistive technology from recognizing the widget's interaction model. Indicator buttons lack programmatic active state, forcing reliance on CSS alone. These are not preference issues; they are structural gaps that break the assistive technology interaction contract for carousels. **REVISE** is required to implement the complete APG Carousel pattern before shipping.\n\n---\n\n### Open Questions (unscored)\n- Is this carousel intended to be auto-playing? If so, does it pause on focus/hover and provide a visible pause/play control? (WCAG 2.2.2 Pause, Stop, Hide)\n- Are the indicator buttons expected to be keyboard-focusable, or should they use `tabindex=\"-1\"` with arrow key routing only? (APG Carousel pattern allows either, but design must be explicit)\n- Does the parent application provide a skip link or landmark structure that makes this carousel's lack of `<figure>`/`<section>` less critical in context?\n\n---\n\n### A11y Evidence Finding (Major Finding #1: Missing Live Region)\n```\nfinding_id: carousel-missing-live-region\nfingerprint: 8a3f9c2e1d4b7f6a\nsource: src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:14-15\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 4.1.3 Status Messages; WAI-ARIA Carousel Pattern\nsection_508_fpc_context: Not in scope (WCAG 2.2 AA target)\nseverity: MAJOR\nperspective_alarms: screen reader=HIGH, cognitive=MEDIUM\nevidence: DOM contains dynamic <img> with state-driven alt text but no aria-live region or role=\"status\" container. React state updates currentIndex without programmatic announcement.\nreproduction_steps: 1. Mount BuggyCarousel with images prop. 2. Click Next button. 3. Listen via VoiceOver/NVDA/JAWS.\nexpected_behavior: Screen reader announces \"Image 2 of 5\" or equivalent status update when slide changes.\nactual_behavior: No announcement. Alt text updates silently in DOM; AT ignores or inconsistently announces it.\ntrend: new\n```",
